   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SEATINI UGANDA</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Southern and Eastern African Trade, Information and Negotiations Institute (SEATINI) Uganda is a regional non-governmental organisation founded in 1996 soon after the WTO Singapore Ministerial Conference. It happened when people realised that Africa in particular and Third World countries in general were marginalised in the World Trade Organisation&apos;s negotiations.
SEATINI was formed to enhance the capacity in these negotiations of African trade officials and negotiators through technical assistance,and also through extending the trade debate to other stakeholders, especially civil society organisations, the media and parliaments. SEATINI also brings together African trade officials and negotiators, with a purpose of consolidating Africa&apos;s negotiating positions.

SEATINI was born when it was observed that:
- African public policy in international forums is often determined ad hoc, and African governments are mostly takers, not makers, of international decisions that affect people&apos;s lives. Governments often sign international trade agreements without adequate information or analysis. Alternatively, the lack of a clear perception of their interests, they often resort to a simple negative posture rather than make commitments to agreements that mightbe of value to them;
- the private sector is equally badly informed about the challenges of globalisation and the effect of the multilateral trading regime;
- civil society understands the complexities of the international regime but it is often excludedfrom decision-making, both at home and in international forums.

Presently, the organisation has offices in Harare, Johannesburg, Kampala, Nairobi and Geneva.  The Uganda office was established in 2001 and is fully registered with the Ministry of Internal Affairs. The country chapters are semi-autonomous with the country director responsible for reporting to the regional director in Zimbabwe. SEATINI has one board for the whole organisation.

ON THE FINANCE FOR DEVELOPMENT PROJECT: SEATINI Uganda is leading the implementation of Tax Justice interventions in Uganda at national level. This is aimed at influencing fair tax policy reform in Uganda at national level and closely works with other national and subnational level F4D partners.</narrative>
